# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone gets CRLF in the working tree while CI on
# Linux gets LF. Any test that parses source files as text then behaves
# differently on the two platforms -- which is exactly what happened to
# tests/schema-drift.test.ts, where a `")\n"` terminator failed to match
# `")\r\n"` and swallowed the rest of the file.
#
# `text=auto` stores everything as LF in git and leaves checkout behaviour to
# core.autocrlf, so this does not force anyone's editor to change.
* text=auto

# Patch files must keep LF or `git am` can reject them.
*.patch -text
*.diff -text
